(6367838, 942601, 130341, '<td valign="top">Very unique.</td>', 'Very unique.', '2011-03-30 14:25:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367860, 942346, 123601, '<td valign="top">to burly</td>', 'to burly', '2011-03-30 15:09:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367864, 942514, 123601, '<td valign="top">has to be an object</td>', 'has to be an object', '2011-03-30 15:14:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367872, 942329, 129267, '<td valign="top">Lovely tones, grains and texture. I find the composition to be a bit haphazard, the framing seems a bit close, and the slight angle of the filter bothers me. Conceptually, it seems simple, especially with only 3 elements (and a weird handle) in the frame. 6</td>', 'Lovely tones, grains and texture. I find the composition to be a bit haphazard, the framing seems a bit close, and the slight angle of the filter bothers me. Conceptually, it seems simple, especially with only 3 elements (and a weird handle) in the frame. 6', '2011-03-30 15:23:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367875, 943554, 129267, '<td valign="top">Nice shot. The black edges seem so dense, is there a way to thin those down a bit with your lighting? The water on the background pulls me out of the effect a bit, it highlights the scale difference, and makes it seem more unrealistic. I would also try this with green instead of the pink, might come off as more ''natural'' or outdoorsy. Solid 7 from me.</td>', 'Nice shot. The black edges seem so dense, is there a way to thin those down a bit with your lighting? The water on the background pulls me out of the effect a bit, it highlights the scale difference, and makes it seem more unrealistic. I would also try this with green instead of the pink, might come off as more ''natural'' or outdoorsy. Solid 7 from me.', '2011-03-30 15:26:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367880, 943609, 129267, '<td valign="top">To me, this is the equivalent of a thought as expressed via text message. Fragments not worth the full  "OMG, no way?"  <br/> <br/>I''m curious how you broke the penny. <br/> <br/>Crop is good, lighting is good, concept is good. Formally a bit plain/not exciting. Ol'' Abe seems to be leaning backwards slightly, which is making the OCD in me twitch a little bit. Overall a 6 from me.</td>', 'To me, this is the equivalent of a thought as expressed via text message. Fragments not worth the full  "OMG, no way?"   I''m curious how you broke the penny.  Crop is good, lighting is good, concept is good. Formally a bit plain/not exciting. Ol'' Abe seems to be leaning backwards slightly, which is making the OCD in me twitch a little bit. Overall a 6 from me.', '2011-03-30 15:31:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367884, 943092, 129267, '<td valign="top">Can''t be an aircraft engine, it''s missing the doohickey that plugs into the watchamacallit. <br/> <br/>Grain is lovely. Lighting, composition, tones, cropping... everything in this is perfect. My one nit pick, and really, it is a  nitpick, is that it doesn''t actually feel disassembled. It just feels exposed... similarly to if one were to open up a hard drive bay, or clock face. 9. My highest of the challenge.</td>', 'Can''t be an aircraft engine, it''s missing the doohickey that plugs into the watchamacallit.  Grain is lovely. Lighting, composition, tones, cropping... everything in this is perfect. My one nit pick, and really, it is a  nitpick, is that it doesn''t actually feel disassembled. It just feels exposed... similarly to if one were to open up a hard drive bay, or clock face. 9. My highest of the challenge.', '2011-03-30 15:34:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367886, 943311, 129267, '<td valign="top">I think I would have liked this more if I had to guess more at what the original shape was. It could have been an interesting commentary on analog vs digital if you were to place everything and position in a more logical or straightforward manner? Maybe Largest to smallest, or separated by color shifts/tones?</td>', 'I think I would have liked this more if I had to guess more at what the original shape was. It could have been an interesting commentary on analog vs digital if you were to place everything and position in a more logical or straightforward manner? Maybe Largest to smallest, or separated by color shifts/tones?', '2011-03-30 15:36:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367889, 942687, 129267, '<td valign="top">Beautifully low key. Good exposure and highlight/flare control. The dust on the lens (filter?) made me wipe my monitor. In this show, I find the reflections to be a bit distracting. They''re so sharp and in some ways, keep me from being able to settle down and enjoy where the objects start/end.</td>', 'Beautifully low key. Good exposure and highlight/flare control. The dust on the lens (filter?) made me wipe my monitor. In this show, I find the reflections to be a bit distracting. They''re so sharp and in some ways, keep me from being able to settle down and enjoy where the objects start/end.', '2011-03-30 15:40:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367894, 943435, 129267, '<td valign="top">Seeing these phones disassembled makes me want to smash them into little bits and pieces, not sure why.<br/> <br/>I think this could have been taken further, it seems almost default. I can see this being an awesome shot if you reassembled the phone, and then used a saw to cut it in half lengthwise. As is, the composition isn''t doing much, it''s kind of hard to see any real detail. The depth of field makes you focus more on the granite texture more so than the phone components.</td>', 'Seeing these phones disassembled makes me want to smash them into little bits and pieces, not sure why. I think this could have been taken further, it seems almost default. I can see this being an awesome shot if you reassembled the phone, and then used a saw to cut it in half lengthwise. As is, the composition isn''t doing much, it''s kind of hard to see any real detail. The depth of field makes you focus more on the granite texture more so than the phone components.', '2011-03-30 15:44:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367898, 943594, 129267, '<td valign="top">This would have more expression without the two "cheek" pieces. I think I would have placed them on the "eyes" as pupils. With the expression of the eyebrow how it is, it would have given the impression of a wink. <br/> <br/>Formally, I think the gradation in the lighting is a bit distracting towards the bottom since the drive itself is also so dark. I think this could benefit from 1 more light source.</td>', 'This would have more expression without the two "cheek" pieces. I think I would have placed them on the "eyes" as pupils. With the expression of the eyebrow how it is, it would have given the impression of a wink.  Formally, I think the gradation in the lighting is a bit distracting towards the bottom since the drive itself is also so dark. I think this could benefit from 1 more light source.', '2011-03-30 15:47:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367902, 943452, 129267, '<td valign="top">Woah, Cooties on Crack. Especially that googly eyed one in the back. <br/> <br/>cropping is tight, I don''t mind that. I wish there was a bit more focus in the foreground. The glowing lime green in the back draws my eye off everything very quickly. <br/> <br/>On black these things seem kinda creepy/not fun. I think another color that played off the playfulness and still isolates the object would have been better.</td>', 'Woah, Cooties on Crack. Especially that googly eyed one in the back.  cropping is tight, I don''t mind that. I wish there was a bit more focus in the foreground. The glowing lime green in the back draws my eye off everything very quickly.  On black these things seem kinda creepy/not fun. I think another color that played off the playfulness and still isolates the object would have been better.', '2011-03-30 15:50:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367906, 943258, 129267, '<td valign="top">Perfect depth of field, and the color of the red is so wonderful. I love the texture around the edges of the pool, and how it seems to be slightly darker there. I don''t terribly care for the blue cast, but if it changes the red color to something else, I can totally see why you would keep it. Lined paper seems like an odd choice, but it adds more to the image than if it were isolated on white alone. <br/> <br/>I don''t know. I''m trying to nit pick, but I really can''t find much. In the spirit of disassembling things, I wish it had more than three parts. Also, come up with a better title. 8 from me.</td>', 'Perfect depth of field, and the color of the red is so wonderful. I love the texture around the edges of the pool, and how it seems to be slightly darker there. I don''t terribly care for the blue cast, but if it changes the red color to something else, I can totally see why you would keep it. Lined paper seems like an odd choice, but it adds more to the image than if it were isolated on white alone.  I don''t know. I''m trying to nit pick, but I really can''t find much. In the spirit of disassembling things, I wish it had more than three parts. Also, come up with a better title. 8 from me.', '2011-03-30 15:54:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367907, 943609, 123601, '<td valign="top">very colover</td>', 'very colover', '2011-03-30 15:55:07.000000', NULL, 1),
